{%- comment -%}
  sections/ds-predictive-search.liquid — Disrupted Studio search results

  Rendered server-side via the Section Rendering API when the user types in the
  search modal. Horizon's <predictive-search-component> fetches this section at
  `/search/suggest?q=<term>&section_id=ds-predictive-search` and morphs the
  returned HTML into the modal's results container.

  PRODUCTS ONLY, deliberately. Shopify's predictive search also returns queries
  ("Suggestions") and collections, and this section used to render both — so
  searching "plugin" produced three stacked groups, and "all" produced a
  collection row and no products at all. The header menu already lists every
  category, so those groups were noise over the one thing being searched for.
  assets/predictive-search.js now pins resources[type]=product so they are not
  even fetched; this section renders only products regardless.

  Required hooks (Horizon's keyboard arrow-nav depends on these):
    [data-search-results]                       — container the component scrolls
    .predictive-search-results__card            — items nav targets
    ref="resultsItems[]"                        — array of focusable items
    data-search-result-index="search-results-N" — focus index per item

  The card itself is the shared snippet (ds-product-card) in its `wide` ratio,
  so search results stay identical to the homepage / collection cards by
  construction rather than by a second copy drifting out of sync.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if predictive_search.performed -%}
  {%- assign products = predictive_search.resources.products -%}

  <div class="ds-search-results" data-search-results>
    {%- if products.size == 0 -%}
      <div class="ds-search-results__empty">
        <p class="ds-search-results__empty-text">
          No results for &ldquo;<strong>{{ predictive_search.terms | escape }}</strong>&rdquo;
        </p>
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      <ul class="ds-search-results__grid predictive-search-results__list predictive-search-results__wrapper-products">
        {%- for product in products -%}
          <li
            class="ds-search-results__cell predictive-search-results__card"
            ref="resultsItems[]"
            data-search-result-index="search-results-{{ forloop.index }}"
          >
            {%- render 'ds-product-card', product: product, ratio: 'wide', index: forloop.index -%}
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Idle renders nothing: the modal collapses to just the search bar until there
    is something to show.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="ds-search-results ds-search-results--idle" data-search-results></div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Disrupted search",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
